    <node id="Spatula">
      <data key="d0">Spatula</data>
      <data key="d1">item</data>
      <data key="d2">"A kitchen utensil typically flat and broad with a handle; made from materials such as silicone, metal, or wood."&lt;SEP&gt;"A kitchen utensil used for flipping or spreading food"&lt;SEP&gt;The spatula is a versatile kitchen utensil essential for cooking and serving food. Characterized by its long, thin form and a flat rectangular blade, it excels in various culinary tasks, including flipping, turning, spreading, and lifting food. Its design typically incorporates a handle for easy maneuverability, enhancing its functionality in the kitchen. Whether it's a standard black spatula or another style, this implement showcases both utility and a simple aesthetic. Overall, the spatula is fundamental in any kitchen, playing a crucial role in mixing, serving, and efficiently handling a wide range of ingredients.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be used to flip, spread, or lift food.";"N/A";"flip;"flip food;"grasp;"hold;"lift;"mix;"move;"move";flip";grasp";lift";move;move";place";retrieve";serve;serve portions";spread;spread toppings;use</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"keep_away_from_heat_sources;"should_not_be_used_on_non-stick_pans_with_metallic_spatulas;keep_away_from_heat_sources_for_plastic_spatulas";not_for_non-stick_pans_with_sharp_edges"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The spatula is currently situated on a small wooden table, which is located towards the left side of the room. It is positioned in a manner where the handle is tilted upwards, while the flat end rests on the counter in the lower left corner of the image. Initially, the spatula was described as being located on the right counter, but this has since changed, as it is now found on the wooden table on the left. There are no additional relevant descriptions provided.</data>
      <data key="d7">The spatula is a kitchen utensil employed for various cooking tasks like flipping, spreading, and serving food. It should be stored in the right receptacle on the left counter according to user instructions.&lt;SEP&gt;The spatula is a versatile kitchen utensil initially located on the right counter, where it is stored for ease of access but remains unused. It is commonly utilized for flipping, spreading, or lifting food items during cooking, characterized by its long handle and flat blade, typically made of metal, wood, or plastic. In its current state, the spatula is positioned diagonally on a tabletop, resting with its blade on the surface in the lower-left-middle part of the table.

Recently, there was an attempt to move the spatula from its position on the right counter to a receptacle on the left counter, intending to ultimately transfer it to a sink. However, this transfer was unsuccessful due to difficulties in grasping the utensil. Despite these challenges, the spatula's primary function as a cooking tool remains intact, and its current locations along with the intended movement reflect the practical considerations involved in its handling.&lt;SEP&gt;The spatula is intended to be moved from the right counter to the left receptacle.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-1719a68ee00ddb7af0b3ec1cdd6dd669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36c21ce0cac5376fb97197d20a05ec65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-802fe41abcd29068d1cfab2708fb0560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c200ce7eb06ff3e3c2dd1282801f14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fae1e4a0a20d9a09831a9b5d49619d65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a14dd52a4347d928d6c41c9c0ac0e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be286acead4ef1bc70824041a807170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3766328c3cde2e0365b9ffc47d9f6bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b925f80758e59af0292fad540647ac31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-798eb7758d55600cec34d19901420b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42b1a9f96375929c8924886770c9a80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b639cd1c084b9a66144da184b9c32741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c52f295cd0cbfdbfe68b4b29e6768f84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ea0022d19a84caef9943d67d71da06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e4732c09360078976a5ca82ab6343d3</data>
