    <node id="Right Counter">
      <data key="d0">Right Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">"A wooden surface, light brown, used for placing objects."&lt;SEP&gt;The Right Counter is a horizontal surface situated on the right side of a kitchen, specifically designed for various kitchen activities. Made from light-colored wood, it provides a flat workspace ideal for food preparation and the organization of kitchen items. The Right Counter serves multiple functions, including holding utensils and ingredients, and it is the designated location where the spatula is initially placed. Its design and functionality make it an essential component of the kitchen space, facilitating efficient cooking and food handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"place items;serve as a workspace"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The Right Counter is a crucial element of the indoor environment, strategically positioned on the far right side. It features a smooth surface and is equipped with multiple drawers for storage, enhancing its functionality. This counter plays a significant role in the workflow, specifically in relation to the spatula, a vital tool for various tasks involving movement. The Right Counter serves as the initial location for the spatula before it is moved to another location, such as the left counter. Previously, this counter was also the designated location for the screwdriver, although that role has since shifted to the kitchen countertop.

Moreover, the Right Counter acts as the operational base for a robotic arm, which is utilized to retrieve items like strawberries within the indoor space. It is essential to note that, while the spatula is identified at the Right Counter, there are instances where it was not retrieved from there. This underscores the Right Counter's importance in the overall workflow and task management of the indoor environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The right counter has a wooden surface and serves as a surface for activity in the indoor environment.</data>
