    <node id="embodied_agent">
      <data key="d0">embodied_agent</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "embodied_agent" refers to a generalized concept that denotes an agent possessing a physical presence, which enables it to interact with its environment effectively. Additionally, it can be understood as an abstract representation of an acting entity within a specific task context. This duality highlights both the tangible aspect of the embodied agent, as well as its conceptual role in various activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"interact;observe;operate"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Embodied agent refers to the entity that interacts with the spatula and performs the action in the kitchen environment, representing the actor in this scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;The embodied agent is a pivotal entity tasked with navigating and interacting within a kitchen environment. Its responsibilities include observing its surroundings by moving to various locations such as a chair, sink, kitchen counter, and refrigerator. Through its actions, the embodied agent performs essential activities, effectively engaging with the kitchen setting and identifying key components like the sink. The embodiment of this agent as the actor in the scenario underscores its role in actively exploring and recognizing different elements within the kitchen environment.</data>
