    <node id="kitchen">
      <data key="d0">kitchen</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The kitchen is a room or area specifically designed and equipped for cooking and food preparation. It serves as a central space in a home or establishment where various culinary activities take place. Characterized by its facilities and equipment that facilitate cooking, the kitchen is an essential part of both domestic and commercial environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The kitchen is a designated space within a home, specifically equipped with various tools and objects essential for food preparation. It serves multiple purposes, functioning not only as a practical area for cooking but also as a setting for interactions with various objects. In this environment, an embodied agent, such as a person, can navigate to the refrigerator, allowing for observation and interaction with the kitchen's features. Central to its functionality, the kitchen includes key elements such as the countertop, the sink, and often utilizes tools like a robotic arm for enhanced culinary tasks. The kitchen is recognized as the global context for the location of both the left counter and the sink, illustrating its integral role in culinary activities. Additionally, it is within this environment that specific tasks, like spatula placement, are executed, which involves careful consideration of the spatial arrangements of items within the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c601eedff7367685c4571bf3fb4e6897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d003a7dded7e53fc4b8f7d41c6ed25c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37720e0e8670494d882077e0c2fdb0d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0b2ba21d505fd28dd62306ebe7dabc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d09a9faf402d6241ce1f575ca4d6e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81be1e6ebc963331233c20fadd377f38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec35a8ddafd6be77a53ae9f696da899c</data>
