    </node>
    <node id="Sink">
      <data key="d0">Sink</data>
      <data key="d1">receptacle</data>
      <data key="d2">"A sink is a basin made of materials such as metal, porcelain, or plastic, with a drainage system."&lt;SEP&gt;A sink is a plumbing fixture typically found in kitchens and bathrooms, designed to hold water and facilitate various cleaning tasks. Characterized by its large, bowl-shaped basin, a sink is often embedded in countertops and is commonly used for washing dishes, food items, and hands. Made from materials such as metal, porcelain, or composite materials, sinks provide convenience with a faucet, often featuring a rounded handle, to aid in the washing process. They are equipped with plumbing for effective drainage, ensuring efficient cleanup and sanitation. Overall, sinks are essential fixtures that play a significant role in household hygiene and maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Allows for washing and rinsing;"Can be used to wash hands, dishes, or other items.";"N/A";"can be used for washing;"fill;"fill_with_water;"hold_water;"holds water;"made of porcelain, stainless steel, or composite;bowl-shaped;can be filled with water";clean;clean";drain;drain";drain_liquids";drain_water;drain_water";facilitates washing tasks";includes fixtures like faucets.";serves as a sanitary space for food preparation.";use_faucet";wash";wash_dishes;wash_items</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"keep_away_from_children;"must_be_connected_to_plumbing;"not_for_food_storage;"should_not_be_overloaded;"washing;avoid_clogging";can_overflow";cleaning";draining;filling;heavy_objects;regular_cleaning_to_prevent_clogs";sensitive_to_heat;usually_not_moved_frequently"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The entity "Sink" has several associated descriptions that predominantly contain terms such as "N/A" and "currently_unused," indicating a lack of specific information or relevance concerning its current status. The documentation suggests that the Sink is not currently utilized and does not have readily available data. Furthermore, it is noted that the Sink is "not for food storage" and "requires access to water supply," highlighting certain limitations and requirements regarding its functionality. Overall, the information points to a clear understanding that the Sink is not in active use and has specific conditions that must be met for its proper function.</data>
      <data key="d6">The sink is located in the center of the kitchen, embedded within the countertop. It occupies the left portion of the image and is positioned next to a red object. Additionally, it is identified as part of the left counter and has a local relation to the right receptacle. The global position of the sink is noted as being in the left counter.</data>
      <data key="d7">A sink is specifically designed for holding water and is commonly used for washing hands, dishes, and other items.&lt;SEP&gt;The sink is a vital fixture commonly found in kitchens and bathrooms, designed for holding and draining water. This practical object serves as a large bowl-shaped receptacle essential for various household tasks, primarily focused on washing hands, dishes, and other items, thereby significantly contributing to sanitation and cleaning activities.

Typically constructed from durable materials such as stainless steel or porcelain, the sink features a basin equipped with a faucet, making it integral to many domestic environments. In the kitchen, the sink is traditionally positioned to facilitate food preparation and cleaning tasks, often incorporated into the countertop. Its exact location can vary, frequently being situated on the left-most side of the kitchen workspace or centrally placed, but its primary function of maintaining hygiene in food-related activities remains consistent. 

Moreover, observations of daily routines indicate that, despite its crucial role, there may be instances when the sink is not actively utilized, reflecting the dynamics of its usage. The sink is referred to as a receptacle designed for washing, underscoring its practical function within both kitchens and bathrooms. Additionally, in specific kitchen contexts, it is noted that the sink is located on the left counter, where it acts as the final destination for the spatula after being moved from the right counter via a receptacle, further indicating its role in the flow of kitchen activities. Overall, the sink is a central element in kitchen design and functionality, impacting the overall layout and efficiency of domestic tasks.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-36c21ce0cac5376fb97197d20a05ec65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd1939605e599b2e8f3c53f763836e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90bf5638ee3a3fcde326f28275031d19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076095ba2122027b75302f3f5d2337c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88973b588d1feb7be9ea10c1a68d74ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-886662ca03584defff8748507c0de09f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafa3ce59a3a5cce1f123e2ae69b96a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62fd5bc5149a51dfc46863346c5e8c37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e4732c09360078976a5ca82ab6343d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8b3be8b062bd6f0259a3b5b87310e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c52f295cd0cbfdbfe68b4b29e6768f84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9295a03107166f9f5e1bcd702e0107d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d05904a07eecb7b1c5f14ea5377015d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d178dad5c42c696b656b21ab2b6d2aee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3d2ef7b90ecc51fe01d28be313595d</data>
