    <node id="Embodied Agent">
      <data key="d0">Embodied Agent</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Embodied Agent is a robotic or virtual entity specifically designed to perform tasks within both physical and simulated environments. It is characterized by its active engagement with its surroundings, allowing it to perceive, navigate, and interact with various objects and scenarios. This capability not only enhances its functionality but also ensures adaptability across different environments, making the Embodied Agent a versatile solution for a wide array of applications that require interaction within its environment. Its physical representation further facilitates effective task performance, distinguishing it as an active and capable presence in any setting.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"navigate;"navigate";"observe;"perceive;act";detect";navigate";observe"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The Embodied Agent is an entity that operates primarily in a kitchen environment, where it performs various specific tasks such as navigating to a table, manipulating kitchen tools, and observing objects within its surroundings. It can be conceptualized as either a physical or virtual being, demonstrating its capability to interact and respond to different elements present in the kitchen. As an active participant in this workspace, the Embodied Agent is responsible for critical actions including navigation, observation, and interaction with its environment, contributing significantly to the dynamics of the kitchen space.

One of its key functions is tool management, which includes verifying the location of items like a screwdriver as well as attempting to retrieve and manipulate other kitchen tools such as a spatula and a receptacle. Through these tasks, the Embodied Agent identifies and updates its perceptions regarding specific features in the environment, including notable objects like the sink. Overall, the Embodied Agent engages in actions that fulfill its designated role within a task framework, effectively enhancing its operational contributions within the kitchen.&lt;SEP&gt;The embodied agent is the actor responsible for identifying the sink as a receptacle on the left counter.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-0f25348c99f083f8776a2ff0e1e0f6d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076095ba2122027b75302f3f5d2337c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd1939605e599b2e8f3c53f763836e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10ba8da3ef47ad6ee34b78a94deace59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be286acead4ef1bc70824041a807170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-886662ca03584defff8748507c0de09f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f3683717d923b16cff2cf4b6372c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fde43ad2483ca3cce0ed9d1fff41ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-597005f2046052883060cb8d0b574098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ea0022d19a84caef9943d67d71da06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6b53c2b60c482c47280b9bfb98e486</data>
