    <node id="Environment">
      <data key="d0">Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">"Surroundings or conditions in which an entity operates."&lt;SEP&gt;The Environment is described as an enclosed space characterized by the presence of furniture and various objects that facilitate interaction. It is defined not only by the physical items present but also by the spatial context in which these objects are observed. This environment includes features such as a robotic arm, which suggests an interactive or functional element within the space. Overall, the Environment serves as the surrounding context in which agents operate, highlighting the importance of both the objects and the layout in facilitating interaction and observation.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"navigate;"observe;"provides_space_for_living;conduct_experiments";interact";observe"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"limited_by_interior_design;limited_by_organization"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"encompasses entire visual scene"</data>
      <data key="d7">Environment relates to the broader context in which the workspace and laboratory are situated, highlighting structural considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Environment refers to a room setting that incorporates a mix of practical and decorative elements, which are designed to support both living and experimental activities. The organization and design of the environment play a crucial role in determining how it functions and how interactions take place within it. Various essential elements, such as furniture and other objects, are included in this setting. For instance, in a kitchen environment, the countertop is equipped with numerous objects that serve as context for actions performed by an embodied agent. Additionally, the environment encompasses areas like a room that contains a wooden table and several objects, which facilitate navigation and observation for the agent. Overall, the environment serves as a comprehensive setting that includes diverse components such as a robotic arm, a chair, a wooden surface, and paper, all of which contribute to the interactions and activities occurring within it.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-41574791f5173705d0af68bad0eedba1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ca8dbd42a1ba490605848abbde35a0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-870ef109d81ab32053f9af21c1d0a708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a5ed4a89b2aa0297099f4ccbb1618fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b0cc1e0b1f231d87d93c83ec8e6611</data>
