    <node id="Kitchen Counter">
      <data key="d0">Kitchen Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">"A horizontal surface typically used for food preparation and storage of kitchenware."&lt;SEP&gt;The Kitchen Counter is a flat surface commonly found in kitchens, primarily designed for preparing food and performing various kitchen tasks. It serves as a specific type of furniture that holds and organizes various items, ensuring they are easily accessible. This multifunctional surface facilitates food preparation and supports an array of kitchen activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"hold objects;"place items;"support;organize";place;prepare food";serve as workspace for cooking and meal preparation"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"objects should be organized to prevent clutter;heavy items may require careful handling"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"Typically located in the kitchen area; adjacent to other kitchen appliances."</data>
      <data key="d7">The Kitchen Counter is a central furniture piece in the kitchen setting that serves as a flat surface for various activities, including food preparation. It functions as a receptacle where kitchen tools and items, such as a robotic arm, power drill, black spatula, cleaning sponge, and a red apple, are organized and laid out in a distinct arrangement for use. The kitchen counter is essential in facilitating the navigation and interaction of agents within the kitchen environment, providing a designated space for the collection and use of these items.&lt;SEP&gt;The kitchen counter serves as an area for storing tools and utensils within a kitchen, suitable for food preparation.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-1719a68ee00ddb7af0b3ec1cdd6dd669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-870ef109d81ab32053f9af21c1d0a708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f21be762aa6dcf22e2e46bd7c66b1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1fde43ad2483ca3cce0ed9d1fff41ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6b53c2b60c482c47280b9bfb98e486</data>
