    <node id="Left Counter">
      <data key="d0">Left Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">"A flat surface in the kitchen used for various tasks"&lt;SEP&gt;"A kitchen counter that serves as a workspace for food preparation and utensil placement."&lt;SEP&gt;The Left Counter is a dark-colored wooden piece of furniture situated on the left side of the room, specifically designed to serve multiple purposes in the kitchen. It features a flat surface that functions as both a workspace and a resting place for various items. The Left Counter prominently houses a sink within its structure, making it an essential area for everyday kitchen tasks. Additionally, it includes a receptacle and is adorned with decorative items, which not only enhance the organization of the space but also contribute to its aesthetic appeal. Overall, the Left Counter is a significant component of the kitchen, merging functionality with decorative elements, and is characterized by its dark wood finish and the presence of assorted objects that influence the arrangement of items on its surface.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"place;"place items;"place objects";serve as a workspace";store"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The Left Counter is a term referenced in the provided data; however, comprehensive descriptions are lacking as three of the entries are marked as "N/A". Consequently, the available information is limited to the mention of the term "left counter" without any additional context or details.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Left Counter is a designated location notable for its functional and decorative elements. It features a receptacle specifically intended for the transfer of the spatula from the adjacent right counter, highlighting its practical role in the overall setup. Additionally, this counter is equipped with a receptacle for a screwdriver, further emphasizing its utility. The Left Counter is strategically positioned to the left of a robotic arm, optimizing its operational context.

In terms of aesthetics, the Left Counter includes a small dark-colored table adorned with decorative items, enhancing the visual appeal of the workspace. Furthermore, it incorporates a sink, combining functionality with an attractive design. However, the Left Counter is also marked by various obstructions, which have led to failures during task execution, indicating potential challenges in its current setup. Overall, the Left Counter serves as a multifaceted area, fulfilling both practical and aesthetic purposes within the living area.&lt;SEP&gt;The left counter is part of the kitchen setup where various utensils, including the spatula, are placed for convenience and organization.&lt;SEP&gt;The left counter is a designated area in the kitchen where the sink is situated.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-36c21ce0cac5376fb97197d20a05ec65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd1939605e599b2e8f3c53f763836e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4871e034512b0b2f656d2ac6e551a0ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b6b2acc8305133b9f878445cdab5bbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a14dd52a4347d928d6c41c9c0ac0e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be286acead4ef1bc70824041a807170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b925f80758e59af0292fad540647ac31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-543ffef2ab0f0d3ee367be8b0c6e247d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-798eb7758d55600cec34d19901420b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42b1a9f96375929c8924886770c9a80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b639cd1c084b9a66144da184b9c32741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3d2ef7b90ecc51fe01d28be313595d</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
