    <node id="Wooden Counter">
      <data key="d0">Wooden Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">The Wooden Counter is a piece of furniture characterized by its flat surface constructed from wood. It serves various purposes, including as a workspace for tasks and as a surface for placing items. Commonly, Wooden Counters are utilized in settings such as kitchens for food preparation and in other environments where a durable, functional surface is needed.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"hold items;"provides a surface for placing and manipulating items";"provides workspace;may have storage beneath";provide surface";supports items and tools</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"susceptible to scratches;heat damage";water damage</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"Found on the right side of the foreground, it serves as a working surface possibly for preparing food or conducting tasks, and supports a robotic arm adjacent to other objects."&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The wooden counter serves as a multifunctional surface designed for placing objects such as a robotic arm and an exercise ball. It is characterized by a light finish, which enhances its versatility as a workspace in various settings, including kitchens, workshops, and studios. Positioned in the foreground, the wooden counter is mounted under the robotic arm, indicating its functional role in this setup. Additionally, the counter is located within a kitchen environment, where it interacts with other kitchen items, such as a spatula, which is situated on the right side of the counter. Overall, this wooden counter plays a crucial role in supporting a variety of activities and objects.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-fe69edc1fac589e4f6f4d1fc649968ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbd19b552f2796429c56aa27ab89f6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-798eb7758d55600cec34d19901420b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e777f77f816e4ff69eb46597d7711d02</data>
